# Apache RAT exclusion list -- read by tools/ci/rat.sh, the "License audit
# (Apache RAT)" CI job. Every file in the tree must either carry a recognised
# license header or match a line in this file.
#
# HOW RAT 0.16 READS THIS FILE: each non-comment line is matched against the
# bare NAME of a file or directory (never its path) as a Java regex that must
# match the whole name; a matching directory is skipped together with
# everything under it. A line that is not a valid regex (anything starting
# with `*`) is dropped with a warning and tools/ci/rat.sh fails on that, so
# extension rules are spelled `.*\.ext`. Verify a change by running the
# script -- never assume a pattern took.
#
# WHAT MAY BE LISTED: only files that are non-source (configuration, prose,
# data), third-party, generated, or content-addressed (fixtures and goldens
# whose bytes are pinned by a hash). A first-party source file is never listed
# here to make the count zero -- it gets the SPDX header instead, and
# tools/check-license-headers.sh enforces that per file type.

# --- Version control, build outputs and tool caches -------------------------
# RAT honours either -e options or this file, never both, so the usual
# command-line exclusions live here too.
\.git
bazel-.*
node_modules
\.venv
\.ruff_cache
__pycache__
\.pytest_cache
\.svelte-kit
\.astro
dist
# This file and the report the audit writes into the repo root.
\.rat-excludes
rat-report\.txt

# --- Repository and tool configuration (no code; nothing to license) --------
\.gitignore
\.git-blame-ignore-revs
\.gitattributes
\.gitkeep
\.dockerignore
\.gcloudignore
\.helmignore
\.bazelrc
\.bazelignore
\.bazelversion
\.clang-format
\.clang-tidy
\.prettierrc
CODEOWNERS
GIT_COMMIT
.*_KERNEL_PIN
.*\.ya?ml
.*\.json
.*\.toml
.*\.lock
.*\.conf
.*\.example
.*\.env
.*\.default
.*\.service
.*\.tpl
.*\.tmpl
.*\.sln
# deploy/logrotate.d/: logrotate drop-in configuration.
logrotate\.d

# --- Documentation, prose, data and images ----------------------------------
(?i).*\.mdx?
.*\.txt
.*\.csv
.*\.svg

# --- License and notice files (they ARE the license text) --------------------
LICENSE.*
NOTICE
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES

# --- Website content -----------------------------------------------------------
# .astro files are page / component / layout markup, deliberately header-free
# (the repo gate only residue-scans them). website/src/content/ is prose.
# website/public/ is NOT excluded: its first-party demo pages carry the
# header, the archived 1.0 documentation carries the upstream Apache-2.0
# text RAT recognises, and the rest is images, fonts, svg/txt/csv/yaml data
# and the machine-readable .well-known/ metadata (RFC 8615 well-known URIs,
# served verbatim as JSON / plain text).
.*\.astro
content
\.well-known

# --- Generated code ------------------------------------------------------------
# lib/image/generated/: model tables and predictors emitted by the training
# tool; regenerated, never hand-edited.
generated

# --- Generated goldens and byte-exact fixtures ----------------------------------
# Every first-party synthetic INPUT that can carry a header does: the
# JS-minifier corpus inputs (lib/js/corpus/bundle-fixtures/src,
# lib/js/corpus/findings/repros) and the HTML-parse corpus seeds arrive
# headered from the canonical 1.15 tree, and their goldens manifests pin the
# headered bytes. What stays listed, and why: the goldens themselves
# (generated expected outputs — a header cannot go into a file whose whole
# content is the recorded parse); the three seeds whose test IS their exact
# byte content (empty input, whitespace-only input, a document with no
# markup); and the async-css-probe capture of the modpagespeed.com home page
# (tools/async-css-probe/fixtures/modpagespeed-com, byte-frozen, sha256 per
# file in its CAPTURE.md). Ordinary testdata/ directories are NOT excluded:
# their first-party fixtures carry the header and are only ever compared
# relatively (optimized vs origin), never byte-pinned.
goldens
empty\.html
whitespace-only\.html
text-only\.html
modpagespeed-com

# --- Third-party test inputs ---------------------------------------------------
# test/lib/js/testdata: AngularJS, jQuery and Prototype (MIT) as the
# .original/.minified pairs the minifier tests run against.
.*\.original
.*\.minified
